  "notes": "{嗅|か}ぐ means to smell or sniff—the active verb for perceiving odors.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n{嗅|か}ぐ is transitive—you smell something:\n- {匂|にお}いを{嗅|か}ぐ: to smell a scent\n- {香|かお}りを{嗅|か}ぐ: to smell a fragrance\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {嗅|か}ぐ: to smell (active, intentional)\n- {匂|にお}う: to smell, give off odor (intransitive)\n- {匂|にお}いがする: there is a smell\n\nONOMATOPOEIA:\n- くんくん{嗅|か}ぐ: to sniff around (like an animal)\n\nKANJI NOTE:\nThe kanji {嗅|か} combines the mouth and smell radicals.",
